id: pm-vcs-6220
title: "Harden the distribution surface against the review findings: one base for clone, atomic remotes, and a bounded push namespace"
description: "The first review of the distribution tranche found six defects the tests did not reach. A clone resolved its source against the process working directory while resolving its destination against the command's working root, so the two disagreed exactly when a path was passed; it then recorded the location as typed, leaving the clone holding a remote relative to its own root. A failed fetch mid-clone left an initialised repository behind, so the retry met already_initialised rather than the original error. The remotes map was written by truncating the destination, so a crash mid-write left a file that no longer parses and took every fetch, push and remote command down with it. A repeated branch name reached the remote as two updates for one ref and failed there as a ref transaction fault. A push accepted any well-formed ref name, so a sender could move the receiver's record of what a third party published. A file URL naming no local path surfaced as a raw TypeError."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: "area:vcs",distribution,review
created_at: "2026-08-02T23:06:22.571Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T06:26:54.471Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T23:35:01.175Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T23:35:01.175Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "A clone resolves its source and its destination against the same base and records the resolved location, so the clone's own later fetch reaches the repository it came from; a clone whose fetch fails removes what it created and leaves a pre-existing destination's files intact; the remotes map is published by writing a temporary file in the destination directory and renaming it into place, never by truncating the destination; a write that fails before the temporary is created leaves that directory clean, verified by making it read-only; a branch named twice in one push is pushed once; a push refuses any ref that is neither a branch nor a tag; a file URL that names no local path is refused as an unreachable remote rather than raising a TypeError; coverage stays at 100 percent on lines, branches and functions"
parent: pm-vcs-wm40
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T03:15:28.299Z","harness:claude-code","Scope of the cleanup guarantee, after review. write() can fail in two places. Before the temporary exists, which is what the read-only-directory test reaches and what the criterion claims. After it exists but before the rename publishes it, for example ENOSPC part-way through writeFileSync, which the catch handles with rmSync but which cannot be injected portably; renameSync itself cannot be made to fail through the public API, because add and remove both call list first and that only succeeds when the destination is absent or a readable file, and a rename onto either succeeds on POSIX. The catch is therefore defensive for a case no test pins, and the record does not claim otherwise."
  "2026-08-03T06:26:54.470Z","harness:claude-code","Second review round: CodeRabbit found the remote-resolution test supplied one directory as both the repository root and the command working root, so a regression resolving against repository.root instead of sourceWorkingRoot(context) would still have passed it. The test now runs vcs remote from a nested working root and asserts the stored location is that root's ../sibling, with an explicit assertion that the two candidate bases differ. vcs-commands.ts:704 is the site under guard. Coverage held at 100/100/100."
close_reason: "Fixed in the review-hardening tranche: clone resolves source and destination against one base and records the resolved location, a failed clone cleans up what it created, remotes.json is written atomically, repeated push branches deduplicate, a push is bounded to branches and tags, and an unusable file URL is refused as an unreachable remote. 11 new tests, coverage held at 100/100/100."
body: ""
